<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Eryops megacephalus Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 127 µm (Cisuralian, 295 Ma) (Eryops megacephalus)",
        "Eryops megacephalus Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 127 µm (Cisuralian, 295 Ma) faithfully reproduces Eryops megacephalus morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Eryops megacephalus specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Eryops megacephalus" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A later Eryops chronospecies. The series length is 1.",
        "does_not_claim: That 127 µm pits were counted on the AMNH mount.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Pass-1 full-frame composite is the anatomical placement of the pigment.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian, k_c, and an explicit Euler Schnakenberg integrator on a 96x96 periodic patch with lambda_c fixed at 127 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass-1 full-frame composite of that field onto the AMNH photograph (cv_sim_similarity 94.4).",
        "reported_in_source: Pawley and Warren 2006: Eryops megacephalus Cope, 1877 is an Early Permian eryopoid; this slot uses 295 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the quadratic two-species system used as the kinetics.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: reaction-diffusion instabilities select a finite critical wavenumber k_c.",
        "reported_in_source: Witzmann et al. 2010: basal tetrapod dermal bone carries sculptured ornament.",
        "transfer_boundary: 127 µm is the assigned primordium wavelength. The museum photograph cannot resolve it.",
        "transfer_boundary: 8184 = 64*127+56 compares this wavelength to the 8.184 mm organ-scale pit, which is a different slot." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Eryops megacephalus (Early Permian (Cisuralian, 295 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Amphibia & Reptilia (Ootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Eryops" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/eryops_megacephalus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Eryops megacephalus; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: reaction-diffusion instabilities select a finite critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979: the quadratic two-species system used as the kinetics. | Pawley and Warren 2006: Eryops megacephalus Cope, 1877 is an Early Permian eryopoid; this slot uses 295 Ma. | Witzmann et al. 2010: basal tetrapod dermal bone carries sculptured ornament.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian, k_c, and an explicit Euler Schnakenberg integrator on a 96x96 periodic patch with lambda_c fixed at 127 µm. | Pass-1 full-frame composite of that field onto the AMNH photograph (cv_sim_similarity 94.4).; transfer_boundary: 127 µm is the assigned primordium wavelength. The museum photograph cannot resolve it. | 8184 = 64*127+56 compares this wavelength to the 8.184 mm organ-scale pit, which is a different slot.; does_not_claim: That 127 µm pits were counted on the AMNH mount. | A later Eryops chronospecies. The series length is 1. | That the Pass-1 full-frame composite is the anatomical placement of the pigment.]; other sources: Eryops megacephalus skeleton at the American Museum of Natural History <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eryops_megacephalus_skeleton_at_American_Museum_of_Natural_History.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 164 µm (0.0001637 m, log10=-3.786 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 164 µm to 36.8 cm): 164 µm:eryops-megacephalus-bioelectric-polarity, 512 µm:eryops-megacephalus-vertex-packing, 8.2 mm:eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength, 1.6 cm:eryops-megacephalus-clock-wavefront, 3.7 cm:eryops-megacephalus-morphogen-condensation, 4.5 cm:eryops-megacephalus-elastic-buckling, 5.1 cm:eryops-megacephalus-flux-canalization, 7.2 cm:eryops-megacephalus-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1096-3642.2009.00599.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1666/0022-3360(2006)80[561:tasoem]2.0.co;2> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://paleobiodb.org/classic/checkTaxonInfo?taxon_name=Eryops>,
        <https://www.morphosource.org/Search/index?search=Eryops> ;
    pk:fossilLineageGroup "Tetrapod Fin-to-Limb Fossil Transition" ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 2.95e+02 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Early Permian (Cisuralian, 295 Ma)" ;
